<title>USA: Vermont Yankee trims 510 MW nuclear plant output.</title>
<headline>Vermont Yankee trims 510 MW nuclear plant output.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vermont Yankee Nuclear Power Corp trimmed output at its 510 megawatt (MW) Vermont Yankee plant to repair a condensate pump seal leak, Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>In its daily status report, Vermont Yankee planned to reduce production of the Vernon, Vt., nuclear station to 80 percent of capacity, NRC said.</p>
<p>Vermont Yankee is owned by a consortium of New England utilities including Central Vermont Public Service Co, New England Electric System, Green Mountain Power, Northeast Utilities and Central Maine Power Co.</p>
<p>--New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
</text>
